{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928905-i-need-recommendations-on-all-things-wta","id":928905,"title":"I need recommendations on all things WtA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-09T14:24:34-07:00","id":928905,"title":"I need recommendations on all things WtA","content":"Hello there,<br /> <br /> So I discovered Werewolf the Apocalypse almost a year ago by collecting the Rage cards in my local comic book shop. I only very recently found out what it was, a role-playing game, and I'm completely smitten on the concept and lore. I don't have many friends that are interested in playing the game, but I don't care I really just want to start reading and collecting the books. So I ask the veterans here: Which are your favorite novels and/or resource books? Your least favorites? Which ones should I avoid and why?<br /> <br /> So far, my favorite of the novels is Breathe Deeply, but I haven't read any of the World of Darkness books or the &quot;When Will you Rage?&quot; analogies. My favorite resource books are &quot;Book of the Weaver&quot; and &quot;Hengeykai: Shapeshifters of the East&quot;. I haven't read a least favorite yet.<br /> <br /> Bonus question:<br /> My favorite concept in all of WtA are the Skin Dancers what would you say is the best resource for them?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","user":"Story","date":". 07-09-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T14:56:39-07:00","id":928910,"title":"","content":"The W20 Anniversary book should be a good resource for Everything.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, Kinfolk unsung Heroes, or the Upcoming book on kinfolk is good if you want to make skindancers, as the book Pariahs<br /> <br /> Project Twilight is good if you want to see the Government response to the supernatural (Had a problem once with someone I tried showing WTA too INSISTING that the government would have in depth info on tribes and such and coopt their leadership yadda yadda yadda.<br /> <br /> None of that is what happened.<br /> <br /> Hammer and klaive is good for info on fetishes and Talens.<br /> <br /> Way of the Wolf if you want some help making a lupus Garou<br /> <br /> Guardians of the Caerns has some bits on sept life, and what its like and some advise on Metis.<br /> <br /> Book of Auspices is good with lots of gifts, rites and Fluff.<br /> <br /> Book of the City is mostly a fluff book but lets you see the city from a Garous PErspective<br /> <br /> oh the OP Storytellers Handbook, artworks Dated, but it has a VERY interesting optional rule<br /> <br /> Garou get Sick in the city.<br /> <br /> Tribebooks, you'll have to decide which ones are worthy of your money.<br /> <br /> I only bought the ShadowLord and Red Talon Tribe books.<br /> <br /> And the Recently Available White Howler Book, about a decade latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 07-09-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:24:34-07:00","id":928943,"title":"","content":"W20 and W20 umbra should be a good place to start. If you plan on running a game them the W20 book of the wyrm too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T17:38:17-07:00","id":928983,"title":"","content":"One thing you have to remember with WTA is that Western werewolves are behind the times when compared to African or Asian werewolves. The latter groups have united with the other Fera (shapeshifters) to create a united front against the Wyrm. The Western werewolves still think that they can do it on their own...<br /> <br /> Of the Fera, Ratkin have the most potential for weak groups while Mokole have the most potential for strong groups. A Gnosis 10 Mokole can create a rather frightening hybrid form that can resemble Godzilla if they want, while the Ratkin swarm (there are potentially millions of Ratkin, it just depends on how many Kinfolk the Ratkin are willing to expose to the Birthing Plague).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T20:01:33-07:00","id":929026,"title":"","content":"The W20 line as a whole has been quite solid. I recommend getting W20 Rage Across the World. It covers Septs and caerns and what its like within them as well as a variety of locations across the world and number of Totems, Gifts and etc. W20 Umbra is a maybe as while you'll use spirits you may not use the Umbra as deeply and as thoroughly as depicted in the book. Changing Breeds is likewise a maybe. If you like the Fera, the Beast Courts and their African counterparts, it's worth picking up. W20 Book of the Wyrm is another highly recommended book as it collects a lot of knowledge on the various Wyrm-aligned foes of the Garou from Banes and Formori to Pentex and the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> The White Howlers Tribe Book is something I really only recommend for fans of the Tribe or those wanting to complete their collection. Don't get me wrong, I like the book but it's very much a niche thing. It's set at the eve of the Tribe's fall, back in the Roman Empire and the conquest of Britain and unfortunately while the back of the book trumpets 'Ideas for using the White Howlers in a story set in the modern nights' it doesn't actually give much on what a modern day White Howler Tribe could look like. For something they list as a feature, they dedicate a page's worth of material at best.<br /> <br /> The Skinner SAS is good and if you like the Skin Dancers, it features them and their founder, the infamous Samuel 'the Ashtray' Haight. Though its not something I'd use for starting characters and new players.<br /> <br /> Of the W20 fiction, I have all three but have only read the Rites of Renown anthology. On a whole, more stories are good than bad and I absolutely <i>love</i> the story The Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T02:31:55-07:00","id":929630,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm not very fond of much of the stuff that is written in W20 and it's supplements.<br /> <br /> As far as stories go, the &quot;Garou Legends&quot; segments at the beginning of most books contain pretty nice pieces, imo. Especially if you liked &quot;Breath deeply&quot;, then some of the older books from 1st or 2nd edition might be more accurate.<br /> <br /> Basically all the books are as PDF downloads on drivethruRPG.com<br /> <br /> I'd recommend the Player's Guides 1st and 2nd Edition, and maybe Player's Guide to the Garou (which is basically the revised Edition Player's Guide).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:12:59-07:00","id":929884,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm a fan of most of the W20 work, I think a lot of the rule changes were improvements (getting rid of dodge, 10's for specialties counting as for 2 successes instead of a reroll, Mokole getting to evolve their archid forms). So I am in agreement with AkatsukiLeader. I found the earlier editions a bit clunkier for my taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T02:55:49-07:00","id":930260,"title":"","content":"Get as much of the W20 stuff as you can. Especially the W20 Core and W20 Book of the Wyrm. Both are excellent and comprehensive.<br /> <br /> The W20 books are excellent distillations and have a lot of info in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T03:52:03-07:00","id":930268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928905-i-need-recommendations-on-all-things-wta?p=930260#post930260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The W20 books are excellent distillations and have a lot of info in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they now?<br /> V20 was an excellent distillation of VtM. But W20 incorporated a lot of new stuff and of the changes made the removal of dodge was the best, and that was taken over from V20. Fact is, W20 disregards a lot stated in the editions before and is imo less of a distillation and more of a copy and pasting of texts with incorporated changes that were not that well thought through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T05:15:29-07:00","id":930285,"title":"","content":"Uh...right. Anyway, apparently heinrich disagrees with the rest of us.<br /> <br /> Not sure why he needed to tell us that twice but good to know, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T06:27:09-07:00","id":930298,"title":"","content":"I just found your choice of word &quot;excellent distillations&quot; especially inaccurate, in general and in contrast to V20.<br /> Then again posting here is a means of procrastination for me, so I'll probably repeat my statement every two or three days, just so I feel the OP &quot;Story&quot; has been sufficiently warned <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:02:00-07:00","id":930421,"title":"","content":"Some revised books that will help immensely;<br /> <br /> Players Guide to Garou- this is basically the be all end all book about garou. Horoscopes, beliefs, camps, flaws, playstyle guides. Everything is here. Well, everything execpt..<br /> <br /> Book of Auspices- these. This book details very deeply what the role for each auspice is. Only one section that is not as good, is the philodox section. But the Theurge and Ahroun chapters are some of the best takes on those two auspices.<br /> <br /> Hammer and Klaive- A book about fetishes, which also goes into the cultural and social role of these holy objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T15:29:57-07:00","id":930549,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer Revised to W20 as well for similar reasons to what Heinrich stated above.<br /> W20 (to me) felt less like a compilation of 20 years of Werewolf and more like a new edition. Some of the rules changes are nice, but most of those are general 20th Anniversary edition changes.<br /> <br /> For a purely Werewolf game I like the Revised and 2nd Edition Players Guides and the earlier (non W20) Umbra books. If you are interested in the other Changers than best bet is to try and pick up their own books. If you just want a brief overview of them, then I would recommend Players Guide to the Changing Breeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T15:45:12-07:00","id":930556,"title":"","content":"I will say I disliked Players Guide to the Changing Breeds because of a few issues, like Mokole gifts were barely touched on (and repeats were involved in it), and that was also where Nagah doing lethal with their venom came from. I know some people think its an OP starting ability for a breed, but Nagah are also best used for an all Nagah game. It also bugged me when the Players Guide went against the Breed Book material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 07-12-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T22:07:34-07:00","id":931816,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you had a chance to discover this amazing weird creation. You're discovering W:TA at an interesting time. As a longtime fan, here's some of my favorites and other recommendations:<br /> <br /> Fiction: The tribe novel series is probably my all-time favorite fiction in W:TA, but it can be hard to find some of the books. The Time of Judgment tie-in novel The Last Battle takes place soon after the event of the tribe novel series, but can be read separately, is just as good as any novel in the series, and is still somewhat easy to find at used bookstores and online. <br /> <br /> The other great ongoing fiction in W:TA is the saga of King Albrecht. The second edition main rulebook has a great short comic that shows how Albrecht formed a pack with Evan Heals-the-Past and Mari Cabrah, characters you're probably familiar with from Rage. His story is continued in the novel The Silver Crown, the Revised Silver Fangs Tribebook, and the aforementioned Last Battle. The anthology When Will You Rage has a few good stories, and the newer releases Rites of Renown and The Poison Tree are great.<br /> <br /> Getting away from the fiction, some of my favorite sourcebooks in W:TA are a handful of older books that are usually pretty cheap and easy to find. Rite of Passage will seem a little dated, being one of the earliest releases for W:TA, but it has some decent art for the time, it walks you through a solid Rite of Passage story, and it introduces some elements that continue to be referenced in later sourcebooks. Rage Across Russia is a classic that explains huge metaplot elements concerning Russia, and Rage Across Appalachia is one of the most interesting and charming settings in the series.<br /> <br /> If you have some money to spend, the Player's Guide to Garou, Hammer and Klaive, The Book of Auspices, and most of the Revised Tribebooks are either very useful, great reads, or both.<br /> <br /> Happy hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T22:25:02-07:00","id":931825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928905-i-need-recommendations-on-all-things-wta?p=929884#post929884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'm a fan of most of the W20 work, I think a lot of the rule changes were improvements (getting rid of dodge, 10's for specialties counting as for 2 successes instead of a reroll, Mokole getting to evolve their archid forms). So I am in agreement with AkatsukiLeader. I found the earlier editions a bit clunkier for my taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny. I too loved base 2e and 2e revised for it all.. but kind of got put off when they got into the apocalypse/red eye/perfect metis time frame..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928905-i-need-recommendations-on-all-things-wta?p=930421#post930421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some revised books that will help immensely;<br /> <br /> Players Guide to Garou- this is basically the be all end all book about garou. Horoscopes, beliefs, camps, flaws, playstyle guides. Everything is here. Well, everything execpt..<br /> <br /> Book of Auspices- these. This book details very deeply what the role for each auspice is. Only one section that is not as good, is the philodox section. But the Theurge and Ahroun chapters are some of the best takes on those two auspices.<br /> <br /> Hammer and Klaive- A book about fetishes, which also goes into the cultural and social role of these holy objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved H&amp;K and the Book of auspices.. Also liked the Players guide revised..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viking Funeral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928905-i-need-recommendations-on-all-things-wta?p=931816#post931816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage Across Russia is a classic that explains huge metaplot elements concerning Russia, and Rage Across Appalachia is one of the most interesting and charming settings in the series.<br /> <br /> If you have some money to spend, the Player's Guide to Garou, Hammer and Klaive, The Book of Auspices, and most of the Revised Tribebooks are either very useful, great reads, or both.<br /> <br /> Happy hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage across Applachia and Australia were imo the 2 best in the series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T00:13:54-07:00","id":931867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928905-i-need-recommendations-on-all-things-wta?p=931825#post931825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rage across........ Australia were imo the..... best in the series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...What?....How?....Buh?<br /> <br /> In twenty plus years of playing WtA this is a phrase I never dreamed to hear spoken.<br /> <br /> :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T04:58:54-07:00","id":931930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928905-i-need-recommendations-on-all-things-wta?p=931825#post931825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage across Applachia and Australia were imo the 2 best in the series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to know what you thought was good in Rage Across Australia. (Genuine question.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T13:30:14-07:00","id":932172,"title":"","content":"It was mostly cause of the stuff on the dreamtime and expansion info on the death of the Bunyip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T00:25:09-07:00","id":933296,"title":"","content":"There's one book that has not been mentioned. Apocalypse is an amazing read even if you will never actually decide to run it. It distilled years and years of the game into a number of plausible scenarios of everything going to hell and how the Garou would respond to it. It was also clevr enough to leave things open ended and give you advice and ideas how to make your own epic end to the game.<br /> <br /> I might never end up running it, but surely the book is one of the best ever written for Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T08:19:40-07:00","id":933429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/928905-i-need-recommendations-on-all-things-wta?p=933296#post933296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one book that has not been mentioned. Apocalypse is an amazing read even if you will never actually decide to run it. It distilled years and years of the game into a number of plausible scenarios of everything going to hell and how the Garou would respond to it. It was also clevr enough to leave things open ended and give you advice and ideas how to make your own epic end to the game.<br /> <br /> I might never end up running it, but surely the book is one of the best ever written for Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the Time of Judgement books for the Big Three aren't as bad as people make them out to be. They have flaws of course but there's a lot of really good nuggets. It's no <i>Ends of Empire</i> butthey're not bad either. Certainly they're better than the waste that is <i>Time of Judgement</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T17:12:04-07:00","id":933655,"title":"","content":"I like the various changing breed books myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T23:06:57-07:00","id":933752,"title":"","content":"Of the breedbooks, the Annassi, Gurahl, Mokole, and Ratkin were my top 4. Closely followed by Bastet, then Rokea, then Nuwisha and Corax pulling up the low end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}